{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1294331-advice-on-a-scion-setting","id":1294331,"title":"Advice on a Scion Setting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-05T23:15:20-08:00","id":1294331,"title":"Advice on a Scion Setting","content":"I am waiting for Scion 2ed to come out. In the mean time, i am planning out a setting for the game that is inspired by 60s spy thrillers, more specifically The Connery Bond Films and a bit of 30s two-fisted pulp. The whole setting would be set in the 1960s-1990s and would focus on PCs, who are on the Origin to Hero level being recruited by the enigmatic &quot;Foundation&quot;, a espionage group led by the equally mysterious Wayne Kaufman. The supposed goal of the Foundation is to fight &quot;extraordinary&quot; threats to the world. By extraordinary, the PCs would mostly be encountering evil megalomaniacs using Mythic Science, insane or evil scions, rampaging Titanspawn, and most commonly, a SPECTRE-like organization called DRAGON. As the chronicle continues, the PCs will learn major secrets about both DRAGON and The Foundation and their leadership.<br /> <br /> Would like some advice on making some of the more common tropes in classical Bondian adventures like car chases work in Scion. I would also like some advice detailing The Foundation and DRAGON and what type of Scions would work for those organizations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 03-06-2019, 02:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T03:37:59-08:00","id":1294353,"title":"","content":"Trinity Continuum have all you need on rules and it is the same system. Of course it\u2019s not available yet...<br /> <br /> For vehicle, there are a lot of rules, but, you can treat them basically as large scale characters, doing Pilot testes instead of Athletics. Add some secret guns in it (goes over the 3 tags rule, put like 1 extra tag for every scale up).<br /> <br /> The focus on Storypath is good narrative and flexible rules, so Improvise, Adapt, Overcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T08:02:18-08:00","id":1294402,"title":"","content":"Assuming this isn't already directly inspired by the SCP Foundation, you should check out the SCP Wiki for ideas about titans/titanspawn in the form of anomalous entities, various groups of interest for organizational inspiration, and some of the consistent, named Researchers/Agents/Etc. for scion ideas.","signature":"","edit